    "updated_at": "2026-11-27T17:31:59Z",
    "body": "The cause is the runner, not the code. No code change can fix it.\n\nEvidence:\n- The run 46033295171 ran on the runner `Hammer-new`.\n- The gate log `1230-clippy_-D_warnings.log` in the artifact `gate-logs-post-merge-46033295171-1` has this text:\n  ```\n  error: 'cargo-clippy' is not installed for the toolchain 'stable-x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu'.\n  help: run `rustup component add clippy` to install it\n  ```\n- That is why the step failed in 1 s.\n- The green run 46029846130 ran on the runner `cheese`. Its clippy step passed in 55 s.\n- I ran the same clippy command on upstream/main `751a79b20` (macOS, rustc 1.100.0). It passed with no warnings.\n\nFix (runner owner):\n- On `Hammer-new`, run `rustup component add clippy` for the user of the runner service.\n\nAn alternative is a `rust-toolchain.toml` with `components = [\"clippy\"]`, or a step in `.github/workflows/post-merge.yml`. Those are process and CI changes. They need the maintainer's decision, so I did not make them.\n\nThe next green run on `Hammer-new` closes this issue. I release the claim. I opened no PR.\n",
    "author_association": "COLLABORATOR",
